IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa24-identity.l4: Part 35 "Identity verification" and "Discrepancy reporting", ss 1110A to 1110D of the Companies
-- Act 2006 (lines 15873-15940 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ANSWERS FOR THE OTHER PARTS. The plan's seam `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` is
-- answered by `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` (MAYBE BOOLEAN: coa1 ss 12 and 12B, coa4 ss 167G and
-- 167M, coa17 ss 790LB to 790LS and coa23 ask it).
--
-- THE SECRETARY OF STATE'S REGULATIONS ARE NOT IN THE SOURCES. ss 1110A(4), (6), (7), 1110B(1)-(3), (5), (6) and
-- 1110D(1)-(4), (7) are powers to make regulations: machinery, listed in NOTES.md as inert (reason 2). What the Act
-- itself lays down for those regulations (the punishments they must provide for, the ceilings on imprisonment) and
-- what a person can state about the outcome (whether a statement has been delivered, whether the individual has
-- ceased to be verified by virtue of regulations) is encoded below, and the regulations' own content is an input.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST x is the text's
-- answer; NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why, as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`); JUST FALSE is the text
-- saying no in its own words (each such branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`).

§ `Part 35: identity verification and discrepancy reporting (ss 1110A to 1110D)`

-- ---- s 1110A ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15875 | (1) For the purposes of this Act an individual’s “identity is verified” if—
-- src:15876 | (a) the individual’s identity has been verified by the registrar in accordance with regulations under section 1110B, or
-- src:15877 | (b) a verification statement in respect of the individual has been delivered to the registrar,
-- src:15878 | and the individual has not, since then, ceased to be an individual whose identity is verified by virtue of regulations under subsection (6).
@ref s 1110A(1) Meaning of "identity is verified" (src:15875-15878)
GIVEN `the individual's identity has been verified by the registrar in accordance with regulations under section 1110B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a verification statement in respect of the individual has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has since ceased to be an individual whose identity is verified by virtue of regulations under subsection (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` MEANS
    IF       `the individual's identity has been verified by the registrar in accordance with regulations under section 1110B`
          OR `a verification statement in respect of the individual has been delivered to the registrar`
    THEN CONSIDER `the individual has since ceased to be an individual whose identity is verified by virtue of regulations under subsection (6)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and the individual has not, since then, ceased to be an individual whose identity is verified by virtue of regulations under subsection (6)"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations under subsection (6) have ended the verification is not in the sources
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of this Act an individual’s “identity is verified” if— (a) the individual’s identity has been verified by the registrar ... or (b) a verification statement in respect of the individual has been delivered to the registrar"

-- src:15879 | (2) A verification statement is a statement by an authorised corporate service provider confirming that it has verified an individual’s identity in accordance with regulations under section 1110B.
@ref s 1110A(2) A verification statement (src:15879)
GIVEN `the statement is made by an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it confirms that the provider has verified an individual's identity in accordance with regulations under section 1110B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110A(2) the statement is a verification statement` MEANS
    IF `the statement is made by an authorised corporate service provider` AND `it confirms that the provider has verified an individual's identity in accordance with regulations under section 1110B`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A verification statement is a statement by an authorised corporate service provider confirming that it has verified an individual’s identity in accordance with regulations under section 1110B"

-- src:15880 | (3) A verification statement must also specify the authorised corporate service provider’s supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations.
@ref s 1110A(3) A verification statement must also specify the supervisory authority (src:15880)
GIVEN `the statement specifies the authorised corporate service provider's supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110A(3) the verification statement meets the requirement to specify the supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF `the statement specifies the authorised corporate service provider's supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A verification statement must also specify the authorised corporate service provider’s supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations"

-- src:15882 | (5) Where a person is required or authorised by any other provision to deliver a statement to the registrar that an individual’s identity is verified, that statement may be delivered at the same time as the verification statement by virtue of which the individual becomes someone whose identity is verified under subsection (1)(b).
@ref s 1110A(5) A statement required elsewhere may be delivered at the same time (src:15882)
GIVEN `a person is required or authorised by another provision to deliver a statement to the registrar that an individual's identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110A(5) the statement may be delivered at the same time as the verification statement` MEANS
    IF `a person is required or authorised by another provision to deliver a statement to the registrar that an individual's identity is verified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person is required or authorised by any other provision to deliver a statement to the registrar that an individual’s identity is verified"

-- s 1110A(9): the two terms the section borrows from the Money Laundering Regulations.
-- src:15890 | (9) In this section—
-- src:15891 | “Money Laundering Regulations” means the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692);
-- src:15892 | “supervisory authority” means an authority that is a supervisory authority under the Money Laundering Regulations (see regulation 7 of those Regulations).
@ref s 1110A(9) "Money Laundering Regulations" and "supervisory authority" (src:15890-15892)
`s 1110A(9) the Money Laundering Regulations` MEANS "the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692)"

@ref s 1110A(9) "supervisory authority" (src:15892)
GIVEN `the authority is a supervisory authority under the Money Laundering Regulations (regulation 7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110A(9) the authority is a supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF `the authority is a supervisory authority under the Money Laundering Regulations (regulation 7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“supervisory authority” means an authority that is a supervisory authority under the Money Laundering Regulations"

-- ---- s 1110B ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 1110B(4): the regulations "must provide for any such offence to be punishable" in the ways listed. The answer is the
-- Penalty of the core, by mode of conviction. "the general limit in a magistrates' court" is not stated in the Act (it is an
-- input), so for summary conviction in England and Wales a caller that does not supply it gets NOTHING.
-- src:15899 | (4) The regulations must provide for any such offence to be punishable—
-- src:15900 | (a) on conviction on indictment, by imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:15901 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:15902 | (i) in England and Wales, by imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or a fine (or both);
-- src:15903 | (ii) in Scotland, by imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both) and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fifth of the statutory maximum;
-- src:15904 | (iii) in Northern Ireland, by imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both) and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fifth of the statutory maximum.
@ref s 1110B(4) The punishment the regulations must provide for (src:15899-15904)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court` IS A MAYBE Period
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1110B(4) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 2, Years)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) divides summary conviction into England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        CONSIDER `the general limit in a magistrates' court`
        WHEN JUST limit THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST limit
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the general limit in a magistrates’ court" is not stated in the Act
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 12, Months)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 0.2)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 0.2)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)

-- ---- s 1110C ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15908 | (1) The Secretary of State may, by written notice given to a person, provide for one or more of the effects listed in subsection (2) to apply in relation to the person, if satisfied that to do so is necessary—
-- src:15909 | (a) in the interests of national security, or
-- src:15910 | (b) for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime.
@ref s 1110C(1) The Secretary of State's power to give notice (src:15908-15910)
GIVEN `satisfied that giving the notice is necessary in the interests of national security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `satisfied that giving the notice is necessary for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110C(1) the Secretary of State may give the notice` MEANS
    IF `satisfied that giving the notice is necessary in the interests of national security` OR `satisfied that giving the notice is necessary for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if satisfied that to do so is necessary— (a) in the interests of national security, or (b) for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime"

-- The six effects a notice may provide for, one constructor each.
DECLARE `s 1110C(2) effect of the notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 1110C(2)(a) section 12(2A) does not require a statement for the person named as a director`
    `s 1110C(2)(b) section 167G(3)(c) does not apply to the notice of the person having become a director`
    `s 1110C(2)(c) section 167M does not apply in relation to the person`
    `s 1110C(2)(d) section 167N(1) does not apply in relation to the person`
    `s 1110C(2)(e) section 1067A does not apply to the delivery of documents by the person`
    `s 1110C(2)(f) section 1098B(2)(c) does not apply in relation to the person`

-- src:15911 | (2) The effects for which the notice may provide are that—
-- src:15912 | (a) where a statement of proposed officers names the person as a director, section 12(2A) does not require a statement under that subsection to be made in relation to the person;
-- src:15913 | (b) section 167G(3)(c) does not apply in relation to a notice of the person having become a director;
-- src:15914 | (c) section 167M(1) does not apply in relation to the person and section 167M(2) does not impose any obligation on a company in relation to the person;
-- src:15915 | (d) section 167N(1) does not apply in relation to the person;
-- src:15916 | (e) section 1067A does not apply in relation to the delivery of documents to the registrar by the person on their own behalf or on behalf of another;
-- src:15917 | (f) section 1098B(2)(c) does not apply in relation to the person.
@ref s 1110C(2) The effects for which the notice may provide (src:15911-15917)
GIVEN effect IS A `s 1110C(2) effect of the notice`
      `the notice given to the person provides for the effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110C(2) the effect applies in relation to the person` MEANS
    IF `the notice given to the person provides for the effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The effects for which the notice may provide are that"

-- Which provision of the Act each effect concerns (the section number as the text gives it).
@ref s 1110C(2) The provision each effect concerns (src:15912-15917)
GIVEN effect IS A `s 1110C(2) effect of the notice`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 1110C(2) the provision the effect concerns` MEANS
    CONSIDER effect
    WHEN `s 1110C(2)(a) section 12(2A) does not require a statement for the person named as a director` THEN "section 12(2A)"
    WHEN `s 1110C(2)(b) section 167G(3)(c) does not apply to the notice of the person having become a director` THEN "section 167G(3)(c)"
    WHEN `s 1110C(2)(c) section 167M does not apply in relation to the person` THEN "section 167M"
    WHEN `s 1110C(2)(d) section 167N(1) does not apply in relation to the person` THEN "section 167N(1)"
    WHEN `s 1110C(2)(e) section 1067A does not apply to the delivery of documents by the person` THEN "section 1067A"
    WHEN `s 1110C(2)(f) section 1098B(2)(c) does not apply in relation to the person` THEN "section 1098B(2)(c)"

-- src:15918 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:15919 | (a) “crime” means conduct which—
-- src:15920 | (i) constitutes a criminal offence, or
-- src:15921 | (ii) is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence, and
-- src:15922 | (b) crime is “serious” if—
-- src:15923 | (i) the offence which is or would be constituted by the conduct is an offence for which the maximum sentence (in any part of the United Kingdom) is imprisonment for 3 years or more, or
-- src:15924 | (ii) the conduct involves the use of violence, results in substantial financial gain or is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose.
@ref s 1110C(3)(a) Definitions for subsection (1)(b): "crime" (src:15918-15924)
GIVEN `the conduct constitutes a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110C(3)(a) the conduct is crime` MEANS
    IF `the conduct constitutes a criminal offence` OR `the conduct is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“crime” means conduct which— (i) constitutes a criminal offence, or (ii) is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence"

@ref s 1110C(3)(b) crime is "serious" (src:15922-15924)
GIVEN `the maximum sentence for the offence in any part of the United Kingdom, in years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
      `the conduct involves the use of violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct results in substantial financial gain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110C(3)(b) the crime is serious` MEANS
    IF       `the maximum sentence for the offence in any part of the United Kingdom, in years of imprisonment` AT LEAST 3
          OR `the conduct involves the use of violence`
          OR `the conduct results in substantial financial gain`
          OR `the conduct is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "crime is “serious” if— (i) the offence ... is an offence for which the maximum sentence (in any part of the United Kingdom) is imprisonment for 3 years or more, or (ii) the conduct involves the use of violence, results in substantial financial gain or is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose"

-- ---- s 1110D ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15927 | (1) The Secretary of State may by regulations impose requirements on a person who is carrying on business in the United Kingdom (a “relevant person”)—
@ref s 1110D(1) A "relevant person" (src:15927)
GIVEN `the person is carrying on business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110D(1) the person is a relevant person` MEANS
    IF `the person is carrying on business in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person who is carrying on business in the United Kingdom (a “relevant person”)"

-- s 1110D(5): "The regulations may not provide for an offence ... to be punishable with imprisonment for a period
-- exceeding" 2 years on indictment, 3 months on summary conviction. Above the ceiling is the text's no; at or below it
-- the text does not say the regulations may (it only bars more).
-- src:15936 | (5) The regulations may not provide for an offence created by the regulations to be punishable with imprisonment for a period exceeding—
-- src:15937 | (a) in the case of conviction on indictment, 2 years;
-- src:15938 | (b) in the case of summary conviction, 3 months.
@ref s 1110D(5) The ceilings on imprisonment in the regulations (src:15936-15938)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110D(5) the regulations may provide for imprisonment of this term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        IF `term of imprisonment in months` GREATER THAN 24
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The regulations may not provide for an offence created by the regulations to be punishable with imprisonment for a period exceeding— (a) in the case of conviction on indictment, 2 years"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars a period exceeding 2 years and does not itself grant imprisonment up to it
    OTHERWISE
        IF `term of imprisonment in months` GREATER THAN 3
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of summary conviction, 3 months"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars a period exceeding 3 months and does not itself grant imprisonment up to it

-- src:15939 | (6) In this section “customer”, in relation to a person carrying out estate agency work, includes a purchaser (as well as a seller).
@ref s 1110D(6) "customer" includes a purchaser (src:15939)
GIVEN `the relevant person is carrying out estate agency work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a purchaser (as well as a seller)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110D(6) the person is a customer` MEANS
    IF `the relevant person is carrying out estate agency work` AND `the person is a purchaser (as well as a seller)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“customer”, in relation to a person carrying out estate agency work, includes a purchaser (as well as a seller)"
